<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Widget/BS<</W 0>>/F 4/FT/Btn/Ff 65536/MK<</BC[0 0 0 0]>>/P 217 0 R/Rect[127.698 405.64799 467.77799 745.488]/T(Figure2)/TU(Diagram illustrating the effects of hypoxia at high altitudes on the human body, featuring blood-brain barrier disruption, increased cerebral and capillary pressure, and various physiological responses, including pulmonary vasoconstriction and hypertension. The process involves AMS \(Acute Mountain Sickness\), HACE \(High Altitude Cerebral Edema\), and HAPE \(High Altitude Pulmonary Edema\), with background imagery of mountains. Arrows indicate flow and interaction between different conditions and body parts.)>>
